{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nm=json.load(open('../audit-spec/v4.json'))\nfor k in ['behaviors','facts']:\n print(k)\n for x in m[k]:\n  if x['id'] in ['B_READY','B_PROPOSE','B_ELECT','B_CONFIG','F_LEADER_COMMIT']: print(json.dumps(x,indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"behaviors\n{\n  \"id\": \"B_PROPOSE\",\n  \"primary_activity\": \"A1\",\n  \"execution_owner\": \"raft.stepLeader / appendEntry\",\n  \"protocol_context\": \"One raft instance, current leader term and active tracker configuration\",\n  \"trigger\": \"MsgProp from RawNode.Propose or forwarded proposal\",\n  \"legal_preconditions\": [],\n  \"implementation_guards\": [\n    \"Reject empty entries by panic; drop when local progress absent or transfer active; appendEntry enforces uncommitted size limit.\",\n    \"Configuration proposals can be converted to empty normal entries for pending or incompatible joint changes unless validation disabled.\"\n  ],\n  \"reads\": [],\n  \"writes\": [\n    \"Assign current term and consecutive indices; append to unstable log; schedule durable self acknowledgment and broadcast.\"\n  ],\n  \"durable_effects\": [],\n  \"external_effects\": [],\n  \"important_branches\": [\n    \"A follower forwards only with known leader and forwarding enabled; candidates drop proposals.\"\n  ],\n  \"async_boundaries\": [\n    \"Self MsgAppResp is queued in msgsAfterAppend.\"\n  ],\n  \"produces_fact_ids\": [\n    \"F_LOCAL_APPEND\"\n  ],\n  \"consumes_fact_ids\": [],\n  \"cross_activity_effects\": {},\n  \"existing_protections\": [],\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"src_raw_entry\",\n    \"src_leader_proposal\",\n    \"src_reset\",\n    \"src_election\",\n    \"src_replication\"\n  ],\n  \"unknowns\": []\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"B_ELECT\",\n  \"primary_activity\": \"A2\",\n  \"execution_owner\": \"raft.hup / campaign / stepCandidate / ProgressTracker\",\n  \"protocol_context\": \"Candidate or pre-candidate role, local term and active voter sets\",\n  \"trigger\": \"Election tick, Campaign, vote response or follower TimeoutNow\",\n  \"legal_preconditions\": [],\n  \"implementation_guards\": [\n    \"hup requires promotable node and no unapplied committed config changes.\",\n    \"Vote grants require canVote and log up-to-date; actual log comparison orders term before index.\",\n    \"Candidate accepts only corresponding response type; first vote per ID recorded and active voter majorities decide.\"\n  ],\n  \"reads\": [],\n  \"writes\": [\n    \"Pre-candidate preserves term and Vote; candidate increments term and sets self Vote.\",\n    \"Winning real election installs leader handlers, resets progress, appends current-term empty entry and broadcasts.\"\n  ],\n  \"durable_effects\": [],\n  \"external_effects\": [],\n  \"important_branches\": [],\n  \"async_boundaries\": [\n    \"Self vote response is delayed through msgsAfterAppend.\"\n  ],\n  \"produces_fact_ids\": [\n    \"F_LEADER_ROLE\"\n  ],\n  \"consumes_fact_ids\": [],\n  \"cross_activity_effects\": {},\n  \"existing_protections\": [],\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"src_election\",\n    \"src_transfer_roles\",\n    \"src_step\",\n    \"src_tracker\",\n    \"src_majority\",\n    \"src_quorum_joint\",\n    \"src_cfg_activation\",\n    \"src_startup\",\n    \"src_snapshot_restore\",\n    \"src_changer\"\n  ],\n  \"unknowns\": []\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"B_CONFIG\",\n  \"primary_activity\": \"A4\",\n  \"execution_owner\": \"raft.applyConfChange / switchToConfig\",\n  \"protocol_context\": \"Application-selected configuration entry or restored ConfState\",\n  \"trigger\": \"RawNode.ApplyConfChange\",\n  \"legal_preconditions\": [],\n  \"implementation_guards\": [\n    \"Simple changes require at most one voter set difference and a nonempty incoming voter set. Joint entry copies old incoming voters to outgoing; leaving joint removes outgoing-only progress and activates staged learners.\",\n    \"Changer copies config and progress before mutations, checks progress for all configured members and learner/voter disjointness. Existing progress, including Match, survives promotion/demotion while fully removed progress is deleted. New progress starts Match=0.\"\n  ],\n  \"reads\": [],\n  \"writes\": [\n    \"Choose Simple, EnterJoint or LeaveJoint changer; replace tracker Config and Progress; refresh local learner flag.\",\n    \"Application acknowledgment can propose automatic joint exit once applied reaches pendingConfIndex and local role is leader.\"\n  ],\n  \"durable_effects\": [],\n  \"external_effects\": [],\n  \"important_branches\": [],\n  \"async_boundaries\": [],\n  \"produces_fact_ids\": [],\n  \"consumes_fact_ids\": [\n    \"F_MATCH\"\n  ],\n  \"cross_activity_effects\": {\n    \"A1\": \"Re-evaluates commit under changed voter sets using retained progress.\",\n    \"A2\": \"May step down removed/demoted leader if configured; aborts transfer to nonvoter.\"\n  },\n  \"existing_protections\": [],\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"src_raw_entry\",\n    \"src_cfg_activation\",\n    \"src_changer\",\n    \"src_restore_config\",\n    \"src_applied\"\n  ],\n  \"unknowns\": []\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"B_READY\",\n  \"primary_activity\": \"A5\",\n  \"execution_owner\": \"RawNode.readyWithoutAccept / acceptReady\",\n  \"protocol_context\": \"Accepted Ready and application progress in one RawNode\",\n  \"trigger\": \"Caller obtains Ready\",\n  \"legal_preconditions\": [],\n  \"implementation_guards\": [\n    \"No committed entry delivery while an unstable snapshot exists, including in-progress snapshots.\",\n    \"Asynchronous mode caps delivery at min(committed, unstable.offset-1); synchronous mode may include unstable committed entries under caller persistence duties.\",\n    \"Application size budget can pause delivery. acceptApplying tracks issuance, not completed application.\"\n  ],\n  \"reads\": [],\n  \"writes\": [\n    \"Expose CommittedEntries; record accepted application frontier; synchronous mode schedules local append/apply responses on Advance.\",\n    \"Advance steps recorded local messages in synchronous mode, then clears them; async mode rejects Advance. StorageApplyResp advances applied monotonically using max with previous applied, frees byte budget and can initiate joint exit.\",\n    \"Node.Advance may be called while external application remains in progress under the Node interface contract; its internal applied frontier is therefore an acknowledgment/bookkeeping frontier rather than independent proof of external execution.\"\n  ],\n  \"durable_effects\": [],\n  \"external_effects\": [],\n  \"important_branches\": [],\n  \"async_boundaries\": [\n    \"Async application responses use term zero because application is not bound to leader term.\"\n  ],\n  \"produces_fact_ids\": [],\n  \"consumes_fact_ids\": [\n    \"F_LEADER_COMMIT\"\n  ],\n  \"cross_activity_effects\": {},\n  \"existing_protections\": [],\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"src_raw_entry\",\n    \"src_ready_accept\",\n    \"src_ready_contract\",\n    \"src_log_delivery\",\n    \"src_log_frontiers\",\n    \"src_raw_advance\",\n    \"src_applied\",\n    \"src_node_application_contract\"\n  ],\n  \"unknowns\": [\n    \"Does the Node early-Advance permission cover a Ready containing a not-yet-activated configuration change, and how do campaign/proposal guards interact with this explicit caller policy?\"\n  ]\n}\nfacts\n{\n  \"id\": \"F_LEADER_COMMIT\",\n  \"meaning\": \"Leader commit frontier has advanced to a quorum-supported index whose entry matches its current term; the prefix is exposed for application separately.\",\n  \"identity\": {\n    \"object\": \"local committed prefix\",\n    \"key\": \"raft instance and committed index\"\n  },\n  \"established_by\": [\n    \"B_COMMIT\"\n  ],\n  \"consumed_by\": [\n    \"B_READY\",\n    \"B_REPLICATION_SEND\"\n  ],\n  \"validity_context\": \"Successful leader maybeCommit under active tracker configuration\",\n  \"representation\": [\n    \"raftLog.committed\"\n  ],\n  \"invalidators\": [],\n  \"reinterpreters\": [],\n  \"durability\": \"In-memory frontier; persistence exported as HardState\",\n  \"recovery\": \"newRaft loads saved HardState.Commit after log/config reconstruction, checks its range, and starts as follower. This restores a frontier from caller-supplied storage without rerunning its historical quorum aggregation.\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"src_reset\",\n    \"src_tracker\",\n    \"src_log_commit\",\n    \"src_raw_entry\",\n    \"src_startup\",\n    \"src_cfg_activation\"\n  ],\n  \"unknowns\": []\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"`doc.go` gives a more explicit permission: `Advance` may occur “at any time after step 1,” before the application step, provided Ready updates stay ordered. The inspected tests use activation before `Advance`, but do not establish that ordering as mandatory. I’ll record this stronger basis alongside the `ApplyConfChange` duty and map the internal acknowledgment consumed by the proposal and campaign guards.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '840,890p' ../agent-source/raft.go; sed -n '1180,1238p' ../agent-source/raft.go; sed -n '477,498p' ../agent-source/rawnode.go; sed -n '63,97p' ../agent-source/log.go; sed -n '326,352p' ../agent-source/log.go; sed -n '112,124p' ../agent-source/README.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '840,890p' ../agent-source/raft.go; sed -n '1180,1238p' ../agent-source/raft.go; sed -n '477,498p' ../agent-source/rawnode.go; sed -n '63,97p' ../agent-source/log.go; sed -n '326,352p' ../agent-source/log.go; sed -n '112,124p' ../agent-source/README.md\"","aggregated_output":"\t//\n\t//  r.trk.Progress[r.id].MaybeUpdate(e.Index)\n\t//  if r.maybeCommit() {\n\t//  \tr.bcastAppend()\n\t//  }\n\tr.send(pb.Message{To: r.id, Type: pb.MsgAppResp, Index: li})\n\treturn true\n}\n\n// tickElection is run by followers and candidates after r.electionTimeout.\nfunc (r *raft) tickElection() {\n\tr.electionElapsed++\n\n\tif r.promotable() && r.pastElectionTimeout() {\n\t\tr.electionElapsed = 0\n\t\tif err := r.Step(pb.Message{From: r.id, Type: pb.MsgHup}); err != nil {\n\t\t\tr.logger.Debugf(\"error occurred during election: %v\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n\n// tickHeartbeat is run by leaders to send a MsgBeat after r.heartbeatTimeout.\nfunc (r *raft) tickHeartbeat() {\n\tr.heartbeatElapsed++\n\tr.electionElapsed++\n\n\tif r.electionElapsed >= r.electionTimeout {\n\t\tr.electionElapsed = 0\n\t\tif r.checkQuorum {\n\t\t\tif err := r.Step(pb.Message{From: r.id, Type: pb.MsgCheckQuorum}); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tr.logger.Debugf(\"error occurred during checking sending heartbeat: %v\", err)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\t// If current leader cannot transfer leadership in electionTimeout, it becomes leader again.\n\t\tif r.state == StateLeader && r.leadTransferee != None {\n\t\t\tr.abortLeaderTransfer()\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tif r.state != StateLeader {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tif r.heartbeatElapsed >= r.heartbeatTimeout {\n\t\tr.heartbeatElapsed = 0\n\t\tif err := r.Step(pb.Message{From: r.id, Type: pb.MsgBeat}); err != nil {\n\t\t\tr.logger.Debugf(\"error occurred during checking sending heartbeat: %v\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n\n\n\tswitch m.Type {\n\tcase pb.MsgHup:\n\t\tif r.preVote {\n\t\t\tr.hup(campaignPreElection)\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tr.hup(campaignElection)\n\t\t}\n\n\tcase pb.MsgStorageAppendResp:\n\t\tif m.Index != 0 {\n\t\t\tr.raftLog.stableTo(entryID{term: m.LogTerm, index: m.Index})\n\t\t}\n\t\tif m.Snapshot != nil {\n\t\t\tr.appliedSnap(m.Snapshot)\n\t\t}\n\n\tcase pb.MsgStorageApplyResp:\n\t\tif len(m.Entries) > 0 {\n\t\t\tindex := m.Entries[len(m.Entries)-1].Index\n\t\t\tr.appliedTo(index, entsSize(m.Entries))\n\t\t\tr.reduceUncommittedSize(payloadsSize(m.Entries))\n\t\t}\n\n\tcase pb.MsgVote, pb.MsgPreVote:\n\t\t// We can vote if this is a repeat of a vote we've already cast...\n\t\tcanVote := r.Vote == m.From ||\n\t\t\t// ...we haven't voted and we don't think there's a leader yet in this term...\n\t\t\t(r.Vote == None && r.lead == None) ||\n\t\t\t// ...or this is a PreVote for a future term...\n\t\t\t(m.Type == pb.MsgPreVote && m.Term > r.Term)\n\t\t// ...and we believe the candidate is up to date.\n\t\tlastID := r.raftLog.lastEntryID()\n\t\tcandLastID := entryID{term: m.LogTerm, index: m.Index}\n\t\tif canVote && r.raftLog.isUpToDate(candLastID) {\n\t\t\t// Note: it turns out that that learners must be allowed to cast votes.\n\t\t\t// This seems counter- intuitive but is necessary in the situation in which\n\t\t\t// a learner has been promoted (i.e. is now a voter) but has not learned\n\t\t\t// about this yet.\n\t\t\t// For example, consider a group in which id=1 is a learner and id=2 and\n\t\t\t// id=3 are voters. A configuration change promoting 1 can be committed on\n\t\t\t// the quorum `{2,3}` without the config change being appended to the\n\t\t\t// learner's log. If the leader (say 2) fails, there are de facto two\n\t\t\t// voters remaining. Only 3 can win an election (due to its log containing\n\t\t\t// all committed entries), but to do so it will need 1 to vote. But 1\n\t\t\t// considers itself a learner and will continue to do so until 3 has\n\t\t\t// stepped up as leader, replicates the conf change to 1, and 1 applies it.\n\t\t\t// Ultimately, by receiving a request to vote, the learner realizes that\n\t\t\t// the candidate believes it to be a voter, and that it should act\n\t\t\t// accordingly. The candidate's config may be stale, too; but in that case\n\t\t\t// it won't win the election, at least in the absence of the bug discussed\n\t\t\t// in:\n\t\t\t// https://github.com/etcd-io/etcd/issues/7625#issuecomment-488798263.\n\t\t\tr.logger.Infof(\"%x [logterm: %d, index: %d, vote: %x] cast %s for %x [logterm: %d, index: %d] at term %d\",\n\t\t\t\tr.id, lastID.term, lastID.index, r.Vote, m.Type, m.From, candLastID.term, candLastID.index, r.Term)\n\t\t\t// When responding to Msg{Pre,}Vote messages we include the term\n\t\t\t// from the message, not the local term. To see why, consider the\n\t\t\t// case where a single node was previously partitioned away and\n\t\t\t// it's local term is now out of date. If we include the local term\n// Advance notifies the RawNode that the application has applied and saved progress in the\n// last Ready results.\n//\n// NOTE: Advance must not be called when using AsyncStorageWrites. Response messages from\n// the local append and apply threads take its place.\nfunc (rn *RawNode) Advance(_ Ready) {\n\t// The actions performed by this function are encoded into stepsOnAdvance in\n\t// acceptReady. In earlier versions of this library, they were computed from\n\t// the provided Ready struct. Retain the unused parameter for compatibility.\n\tif rn.asyncStorageWrites {\n\t\trn.raft.logger.Panicf(\"Advance must not be called when using AsyncStorageWrites\")\n\t}\n\tfor i, m := range rn.stepsOnAdvance {\n\t\t_ = rn.raft.Step(m)\n\t\trn.stepsOnAdvance[i] = pb.Message{}\n\t}\n\trn.stepsOnAdvance = rn.stepsOnAdvance[:0]\n}\n\n// Status returns the current status of the given group. This allocates, see\n// BasicStatus and WithProgress for allocation-friendlier choices.\nfunc (rn *RawNode) Status() Status {\n\n// newLog returns log using the given storage and default options. It\n// recovers the log to the state that it just commits and applies the\n// latest snapshot.\nfunc newLog(storage Storage, logger Logger) *raftLog {\n\treturn newLogWithSize(storage, logger, noLimit)\n}\n\n// newLogWithSize returns a log using the given storage and max\n// message size.\nfunc newLogWithSize(storage Storage, logger Logger, maxApplyingEntsSize entryEncodingSize) *raftLog {\n\tfirstIndex, err := storage.FirstIndex()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tpanic(err) // TODO(bdarnell)\n\t}\n\tlastIndex, err := storage.LastIndex()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tpanic(err) // TODO(bdarnell)\n\t}\n\treturn &raftLog{\n\t\tstorage: storage,\n\t\tunstable: unstable{\n\t\t\toffset:           lastIndex + 1,\n\t\t\toffsetInProgress: lastIndex + 1,\n\t\t\tlogger:           logger,\n\t\t},\n\t\tmaxApplyingEntsSize: maxApplyingEntsSize,\n\n\t\t// Initialize our committed and applied pointers to the time of the last compaction.\n\t\tcommitted: firstIndex - 1,\n\t\tapplying:  firstIndex - 1,\n\t\tapplied:   firstIndex - 1,\n\n\t\tlogger: logger,\n\t}\n\t\tl.committed = tocommit\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (l *raftLog) appliedTo(i uint64, size entryEncodingSize) {\n\tif l.committed < i || i < l.applied {\n\t\tl.logger.Panicf(\"applied(%d) is out of range [prevApplied(%d), committed(%d)]\", i, l.applied, l.committed)\n\t}\n\tl.applied = i\n\tl.applying = max(l.applying, i)\n\tif l.applyingEntsSize > size {\n\t\tl.applyingEntsSize -= size\n\t} else {\n\t\t// Defense against underflow.\n\t\tl.applyingEntsSize = 0\n\t}\n\tl.applyingEntsPaused = l.applyingEntsSize >= l.maxApplyingEntsSize\n}\n\nfunc (l *raftLog) acceptApplying(i uint64, size entryEncodingSize, allowUnstable bool) {\n\tif l.committed < i {\n\t\tl.logger.Panicf(\"applying(%d) is out of range [prevApplying(%d), committed(%d)]\", i, l.applying, l.committed)\n\t}\n\tl.applying = i\n\tl.applyingEntsSize += size\n\t// Determine whether to pause entry application until some progress is\n\t// acknowledged. We pause in two cases:\nAfter creating a Node, the user has a few responsibilities:\n\nFirst, read from the Node.Ready() channel and process the updates it contains. These steps may be performed in parallel, except as noted in step 2.\n\n1. Write Entries, HardState and Snapshot to persistent storage in order, i.e. Entries first, then HardState and Snapshot if they are not empty. If persistent storage supports atomic writes then all of them can be written together. Note that when writing an Entry with Index i, any previously-persisted entries with Index >= i must be discarded.\n\n2. Send all Messages to the nodes named in the To field. It is important that no messages be sent until the latest HardState has been persisted to disk, and all Entries written by any previous Ready batch (Messages may be sent while entries from the same batch are being persisted). To reduce the I/O latency, an optimization can be applied to make leader write to disk in parallel with its followers (as explained at section 10.2.1 in Raft thesis). If any Message has type MsgSnap, call Node.ReportSnapshot() after it has been sent (these messages may be large). Note: Marshalling messages is not thread-safe; it is important to make sure that no new entries are persisted while marshalling. The easiest way to achieve this is to serialise the messages directly inside the main raft loop.\n\n3. Apply Snapshot (if any) and CommittedEntries to the state machine. If any committed Entry has Type EntryConfChange, call Node.ApplyConfChange() to apply it to the node. The configuration change may be cancelled at this point by setting the NodeID field to zero before calling ApplyConfChange (but ApplyConfChange must be called one way or the other, and the decision to cancel must be based solely on the state machine and not external information such as the observed health of the node).\n\n4. Call Node.Advance() to signal readiness for the next batch of updates. This may be done at any time after step 1, although all updates must be processed in the order they were returned by Ready.\n\nSecond, all persisted log entries must be made available via an implementation of the Storage interface. The provided MemoryStorage type can be used for this (if repopulating its state upon a restart), or a custom disk-backed implementation can be supplied.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > retain_advance_map.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nm=json.load(open('../audit-spec/v4.json'))\nfor a in m['activities']: a.pop('behavior_ids',None)\nfor f in m['facts']:\n f.pop('established_by',None); f.pop('consumed_by',None)\nb={x['id']:x for x in m['behaviors']}\nfid='F_APPLIED_ACK'\nm['facts'].append({'id':fid,'meaning':'The local raft instance has processed an application-progress acknowledgment through index i, and its internal applied frontier is at least i. In synchronous Node mode this acknowledgment is generated by Advance; it does not independently establish that the caller executed configuration activation or external application.','identity':{'object':'local application-progress acknowledgment','key':'raft instance and acknowledged log index'},'validity_context':'Runtime processing of accepted Ready completion or local storage apply response within one log incarnation. The frontier is monotonic and bounded by committed; it is not a membership version.','representation':['raftLog.applied'],'invalidators':[],'reinterpreters':[],'durability':'In-memory bookkeeping. Node caller persistence and state-machine durability are separate duties.','recovery':'Startup reconstructs applied from the compacted storage boundary and optional Config.Applied, rather than replaying this runtime acknowledgment. Those initial values are outside this Fact lifecycle.','source_ids':['src_ready_accept','src_raw_advance','src_step','src_applied','src_log_frontiers','src_node_loop','src_node_application_contract','src_usage','src_log_recover','src_startup'],'unknowns':[]})\nb['B_READY']['produces_fact_ids'].append(fid)\nb['B_READY']['source_ids']=list(dict.fromkeys(b['B_READY']['source_ids']+['src_step','src_node_loop','src_usage']))\nb['B_READY']['unknowns']=['Whether the broad Node documentation permission to Advance after persistence is constrained by the requirement to ApplyConfChange whenever a committed configuration is observed. The internal acknowledgment effect itself is established.']\nb['B_READY']['cross_activity_effects'].update({'A1':'The internal applied acknowledgment is consumed by the pending configuration proposal guard.','A2':'The same frontier bounds the committed configuration scan that can prevent campaigning.','A4':'Acknowledgment may trigger automatic joint exit; it is separate from ApplyConfChange activation.'})\nfor bid in ['B_PROPOSE','B_ELECT','B_CONFIG']: b[bid]['consumes_fact_ids'].append(fid)\nb['B_PROPOSE']['implementation_guards'].append('With configuration validation enabled, pendingConfIndex > raftLog.applied rejects a new configuration proposal by substituting an empty EntryNormal; returned ApplyConfChange is not tested by this guard.')\nb['B_ELECT']['implementation_guards'].append('hasUnappliedConfChanges scans only the committed log after max(applied+1, firstIndex); an acknowledged applied frontier controls the scan independently of external application completion.')\nfor p in ['formation','context','connection']:\n path=m['core_overview'][p]\n if fid not in path['fact_ids']: path['fact_ids'].append(fid)\n for bid in path['behavior_ids']:\n  path['source_ids']=list(dict.fromkeys(path['source_ids']+b[bid]['source_ids']))\n path['source_ids']=list(dict.fromkeys(path['source_ids']+m['facts'][-1]['source_ids']))\nm['core_overview']['connection']['explanation']+=' Runtime application acknowledgments also connect completion with formation and authority: synchronous Node.Advance advances internal applied through a queued apply response, while ApplyConfChange separately changes the active tracker. The pending configuration proposal guard and unapplied-configuration campaign scan consume internal applied. Thus acknowledgment is not itself evidence of configuration activation; caller ordering determines whether these meanings coincide.'\nm['core_overview']['open_details'][-1]='Node usage documentation explicitly allows Advance after persistence before the application step, while ApplyConfChange must be called when committed configuration entries are observed. The configuration-specific precedence of these duties remains the focused attribution question; internal acknowledgment and activation are separate mechanisms.'\nfor s in m['surfaces']:\n if s['entry_point']=='Node.Advance before ApplyConfChange':\n  s['behavior_ids']=list(dict.fromkeys(s['behavior_ids']+['B_PROPOSE']))\n  s['source_ids']=list(dict.fromkeys(s['source_ids']+['src_usage','src_readme_ready']))\n  s['reason']='Internal applied acknowledgment and configuration activation are separate source-grounded mechanisms. Node usage explicitly permits Advance after persistence before application; ApplyConfChange also carries a mandatory observation duty. Configuration-specific precedence must be assessed before attributing a violation. Actual policy outcomes are retained in exploration feedback, not this shared map.'\nopen('advance-map.json','w').write(json.dumps(m,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nchanges={}\nfor key in ['B_READY','B_PROPOSE','B_ELECT','B_CONFIG','core_overview','surface:Node.Advance before ApplyConfChange']:\n changes[key]={'impact':'dependency' if key.startswith('B_') else 'clarification','source_ids':['src_usage','src_node_application_contract','src_ready_accept','src_raw_advance','src_step','src_leader_proposal','src_election','src_applied'],'rationale':'Make the internal application-progress acknowledgment an explicit Fact at its actual producer/consumer handoff, distinct from configuration activation. Retain the stronger usage permission and the competing configuration duty.','preserves':'No existing principal Fact is redefined. The self-Match explanation concerns the current-term commit guard; the storage check concerns append-completion history preservation; the paused send-order question concerns persistence before network response. Their requirements, inputs and observations are unchanged by this independent application-acknowledgment relationship.'}\ns={'action':'research','rationale':'Retain the runtime acknowledgment dependency and the explicit usage permission before a later configuration question depends on it. Tests demonstrate common activation-before-Advance policy but do not establish mandatory ordering.','map_path':'advance-map.json','map_changes':changes,'sources':[{'id':'src_node_duplicate_config_test','file':'node_test.go','start_line':279,'end_line':329,'kind':'test_expectation'},{'id':'src_node_learner_config_test','file':'node_test.go','start_line':717,'end_line':773,'kind':'test_expectation'}], 'feedback':{'ref_ids':['src_usage','src_readme_ready','src_node_application_contract','src_node_duplicate_config_test','src_node_learner_config_test','6dab32606865456a91887dbe509c632f'],'answered':'The configuration-specific usage steps sharpen the unresolved premise: doc.go 102-104 and README step 4 explicitly allow Advance at any time after persistence step 1, whereas configuration activation is in step 3. This is stronger than inferring permission from a snapshot example. Node.ApplyConfChange separately says it must be called whenever a committed change is observed. The duplicate-node test activates committed configuration entries before Advance; the learner test also invokes ApplyConfChange before Advance but iterates Entries rather than CommittedEntries, so it cannot independently establish the legal completion contract. Neither test tests early Advance with deferred configuration activation. The map now identifies runtime application acknowledgment as distinct from activation and connects it to proposal, campaign and auto-exit consumers. Exploration 6dab32606865456a91887dbe509c632f remains a conditional observation, not formal Evidence.','remaining':['Assess a scoped configuration proposal responsibility against the explicit Node step-order permission and mandatory ApplyConfChange duty; retain any conflict instead of assuming activation is owed before Advance.','If that responsibility is justified, use the accepted acknowledgment Fact and actual Node producer history to fix a separate formal check with fresh execution. A second proposal encoded as a configuration entry is a narrower endpoint than an inconsistent consensus decision.'],'understanding':'updated','rationale':'The next discriminator is whether the concrete Node policy permitted by the numbered usage steps contradicts the no-prior-unapplied-change proposal promise. This has a source-grounded basis now; repeating the exploratory timing comparison adds no information. Wider safety consequences remain excluded.'}}\nopen('submission.json','w').write(json.dumps(s,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\npython3 retain_advance_map.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_16-15-15-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
